From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:35:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: gemini station: raise the charge
 currents on a wall charger

Name the MT6351 BC1.1 detection's supply to the charger's guard, so a
dedicated charger gets the higher input limit and charge current.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
index e7b849fd8..fa4bcc07d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797-gemini-pda-station.dts
@@ -517,6 +517,8 @@ charger@6b {
 		linux,no-chip-config;
 		linux,guard-battery = "battery";
 		linux,guard-end-threshold = <80>;
+		/* The MT6351 BC1.1 detection module's supply. */
+		linux,guard-usb-detect = "mt6351-usb";
 
 		/* VBUS for the left USB-C port as a host; see the ports below. */
 		usb0_vbus: usb-otg-vbus {
-- 
2.43.0

